Subject: [PATCH] Parse sparse lock annotations in private VM kernel-doc

The runtime PM callback keeps its dev parameter and both sparse lock
annotations. Strip those annotations only while parsing documentation,
so kernel-doc does not mistake them for part of the last C parameter.
Compiler inputs and diagnostics remain unchanged.

--- a/scripts/kernel-doc
+++ b/scripts/kernel-doc
@@ -1747,6 +1747,8 @@
     $prototype =~ s/DECL_BUCKET_PARAMS\s*\(\s*(\S+)\s*,\s*(\S+)\s*\)/$1, $2/;
     my $define = $prototype =~ s/^#\s*define\s+//; #ak added
     $prototype =~ s/__attribute_const__ +//;
+    # Sparse lock annotations are not C function parameters.
+    $prototype =~ s/\b__(?:acquires|releases)\s*\([^()]*\)\s*//g;
     $prototype =~ s/__attribute__\s*\(\(
             (?:
                  [\w\s]++          # attribute name
